commit 58d9f2b9342888d16d1baa1c8e269abea30f33b1
Author:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
AuthorDate: Wed Nov 4 22:03:13 2026 +0100
Commit:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
CommitDate: Wed Nov 4 22:03:13 2026 +0100

    fix(piv)!: use canonical key definitions and explicit protocol subsets
    
    Use Core KeyType for management keys, canonical key lengths and curve OIDs, one frozen wire-ID table with a derived inverse, and explicit asymmetric/management encoders. Preserve unknown management identifiers in nullable mapped metadata instead of guessing a factory type.
    
    Borrow static read-only factory-default slices without renting, filling, or clearing shared material. Name protocol instructions/tags/key references locally, reuse Core status constants, and clarify fallback, MATCH-policy support, and allowed-mode semantics. Clear padded private-component temporaries and use span-based block crypto without extra plaintext copies.
    
    Replace the guessed Bio positional parser and UV payloads with source-pinned TLV and ceremony framing; exercise reordered/malformed metadata, supported-but-unenrolled probes, canonical wire sizes/inverse lookup, unknown identifiers, EC extraction, and default lifetime. Update preview documentation and keep V1 examples intact.
    
    Complexity-Justification: AdminData.TryDecode: Requested type rename only; normalized method body is unchanged from base. Retain explicit TLV schema, flags, and required-field checks rather than combine an unrelated parser redesign with API migration.
    Complexity-Justification: CardholderUniqueId.TryDecode: Requested type rename only; normalized method body is unchanged from base. The flat field/length checks preserve strict CHUID decoding and are existing protocol-validation complexity.
    Complexity-Justification: CardCapabilityContainer.TryDecode: Requested type rename only; normalized method body is unchanged from base. Retain existing mandatory CCC field validation without unrelated behavioral changes.
    Complexity-Justification: KeyHistory.TryDecode: Requested type rename only; normalized method body is unchanged from base. Explicit on/off-card count, URL, and TLV validation remains existing parser complexity.

diff --git a/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md b/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md
index 487f75ee..1f3cb198 100644
--- a/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/src/Piv/CLAUDE.md
@@ -173,6 +173,18 @@ What still needs a human is presence and timing, not destruction — touch-polic
 
 ## Firmware And Feature Gates
 
+Helpers obtain metadata-only category loggers from `YubiKitLogging`, not logger parameters. `KeyTypeEncoding`
+is the sole PIV wire-ID table; its frozen inverse is derived once. Request encoders enforce management vs
+asymmetric subsets, so shared Core `KeyType` does not permit AES slot generation or P-521 requests. Management
+key lengths and EC curve OIDs/sizes come from Core definitions. `KeyReference` holds only internal PIN/PUK,
+management, and Bio references, separate from public asymmetric `Slot` values.
+
+PIN/PUK parameters are named by role and carry caller-owned UTF-8 bytes, not ASCII-only credentials. Internal
+working copies are cleared; shared factory-default key slices are borrowed read-only and never cleared.
+Bio metadata uses tagged fields (retries 06, configured 07, temporary PIN 08); MATCH-policy probes check
+capability, not fingerprint enrollment. Bio verification modes use the Python-confirmed APDU payloads.
+No Bio-hardware coverage is implied by fake-protocol tests.
+
 Use `EnsureSupports(...)` / `IsSupported(...)` from the session base instead of duplicating version checks. Be careful to distinguish device firmware from applet-reported firmware when beta hardware reports sentinel applet versions.
 
 `Features` is a public standalone PIV catalog; `IsSupported` stays public and `EnsureSupports` is protected.
